From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] windows.ui.xaml: Binding, RelativeSource and TemplateBinding objects, a program's own properties

Windows Terminal's tab row showed WinUI 2's own add-tab button, which it hides (IsAddTabButtonVisible="False"), and not its own new-tab button (the TabView's TabStripFooter). WinUI 2's TabView template shows the add button with {Binding IsAddTabButtonVisible, RelativeSource={RelativeSource TemplatedParent}} and the footer with a {TemplateBinding TabStripFooter} that compiled markup writes as an object; both properties are ones WinUI 2 registered for its TabView class. Binding (Windows.UI.Xaml.Data), RelativeSource and PropertyPath are now made: a Binding with a TemplatedParent or Self relative source is set up where it is assigned, as a TemplateBinding is, a Boolean shown on a Visibility as Visible or Collapsed; a TemplateBinding object binds its Property; and properties a program registered with DependencyProperty.Register for its own class are found by name for templates and markup. Compiled bindings (x:Bind) giving a Boolean to a Visibility through XamlBindingHelper (SetPropertyFrom*, ConvertValue) get Visible or Collapsed too.
---
